# English translation (non-binding)

The German text above is authoritative. This translation is provided for
convenience only.

**This is not an open-source license** as defined by the Open Source Initiative,
because it restricts sale. The source is readable, modifiable and
redistributable — just not for money.

**1. What you may do.** *Use it without restriction*, privately or
professionally, explicitly including streams, videos and appearances you earn
money from (subscriptions, bits, donations, advertising, sponsorship, commissioned
work). Whatever you create with the software is yours and you may sell it.
*Modify it.* *Redistribute it free of charge*, provided that: (1) you charge
nothing — no purchase price, fee, subscription, paywall, or bundling with a paid
offering (recovering plain media costs is fine); (2) attribution to the author
and a link to the original project remain and are easy to find; (3) this license
travels with it and your recipient gets the same rights and the same limits;
(4) modifications are clearly marked as such.

**2. What you may not do.** Sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or include the
software or any derivative in a paid product, bundle or service; or place it
behind a paywall or condition access on payment, membership or subscription —
whatever the charge is called.

**3. Author's reservation.** The author retains all rights and may sell the
software, license it differently, or grant third parties rights beyond this
license, at any time. If you need more than this license grants, ask.

**4. Name and marks.** No rights are granted in the name "Pixel VTuber", the
icon, or other marks. A modified version must not present itself as the original
or as endorsed by the author.

**5. Third-party components.** Shipped alongside works of others under their own
licenses — including Electron, Chromium, Node.js (`LICENSE.electron.txt`,
`LICENSES.chromium.html` in the program folder), three.js and the Anthropic SDK
(both MIT). Those components are governed by their own licenses, not this one.

**6. No warranty.** Provided as is, without warranty of fitness, correctness or
availability. Liability is excluded to the extent permitted by law; liability for
intent, gross negligence, and injury to life, body or health remains.

**7. Termination.** Rights granted here end automatically on breach, and are
reinstated if you cure the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it and do
not repeat it.

**8. Law.** German law applies. If any provision is invalid, the rest remain in
force.
